      "id": "texas-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tcss.legis.texas.gov/resources/GV/htm/GV.662.htm",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Texas (Tex. Gov't Code § 662.021) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: the state holidays of §\n662.003(b)(1)-(3), (5) and (6), Confederate Heroes Day (January 19), Texas\nIndependence Day (March 2), San Jacinto Day (April 21), Lyndon Baines\nJohnson Day (August 27) and the Friday after Thanksgiving (Emancipation Day,\nJune 19, is a federal day too). No section of the vendored subchapter moves\na weekend holiday. The Friday after Thanksgiving is listed with `once` from\nthe date the vendored text was retrieved (October 29, 2026) to the end of\n2050. Not modeled: December 24 and 26 (§ 662.003(b)(7), (8)) and the\noptional holidays of § 662.003(c), which § 662.021 does not make legal\nholidays."
    }
